----- stdout -----
Generate configured clients for the current Pina program.

Discovers the project, refreshes its IDL, and generates only the selected client ecosystems. Repeat --client to override pina.toml. CPI-only and Rust-only generation do not invoke Node.js.

Usage: pina generate [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -p, --project <DIR>
          Directory inside the project to discover. Defaults to the current directory

      --client <LANGUAGE>
          Client ecosystem to generate. Repeat to override pina.toml
          
          [possible values: cpi, rust, typescript, dart]

  -o, --output <DIR>
          Override the configured client output directory

      --mode <MODE>
          Override how existing client destinations are handled

          Possible values:
          - auto:      Create clients in empty destinations and update clients in existing ones
          - create:    Require an empty or nonexistent destination
          - update:    Require an existing, nonempty destination and preserve its scaffold
          - overwrite: Remove the complete destination before generating it again

      --no-scaffold
          Generate source files without package manifests or crate entrypoints

      --npx <COMMAND>
          Executable used to invoke JavaScript or Dart renderers. Defaults to npx

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  pina generate
  pina generate --client rust
  pina generate --client typescript --client dart
  pina generate --project ./programs/counter --output ./generated
  pina generate --mode update --no-scaffold

Configuration:
  [clients]
  output = "clients"
  languages = ["cpi", "rust", "typescript"]
  mode = "auto"
  scaffold = true

  [clients.cpi]
  output = "onchain/cpi"

